---
/* ============================================================
   About — mist band
   ------------------------------------------------------------
   Two columns, and they hold two different kinds of thing:

     left    the pull-quote, capped at 560, with the 48×1px mint rule
             32px below it. Shorter than the right column, and centred
             against it.
     right   a 560px block with a 1px mint LEFT border and 40px of left
             padding, so its text measures 519 exactly — 1 + 40 + 519 =
             560, which is why nothing inside it needs its own cap.
             It holds the kicker, both body paragraphs and the stats.

   624 + 560 = 1184, the container's inner width at 1280. There is no
   grid gap to find: the left column takes what is left over, and the
   quote's own 560 cap leaves 64px of air before the mint border. That
   is why the arithmetic closes exactly.

   This band shipped as a single stacked column first. The spec text
   read "below it", built literally, and that left the right half of a
   1184px band empty — logged as OPEN-QUESTIONS.md #8 with the
   two-column reading recorded beside it. The design export settles it:
   two columns, and the kicker sits at the top of the right block, not
   above the quote. #8 is closed for the homepage.

   The two paragraphs are deliberately different sizes — body1 is
   `text-body` (16/26), body2 `text-body-sm` (14/22.75), the
   "secondary paragraph" step. That is what the export draws, and it is
   what makes the second paragraph read as a footnote to the first.

   Below 1120 the columns stack. At that width the left column is
   already down to 464 (1120 − 96 of padding − 560) and a 48px
   pull-quote has nowhere left to go.

   RESOLVED, for the stats: they are side by side (`grid grid-cols-2`)
   at every viewport width, not stacked — a phone screenshot of the
   stacked version was the complaint that reopened this. Their gap
   stays 24, the figure `/about`'s Our Story band was aligned to;
   the export measures closer to 16 and the difference is one step on
   the scale. See OPEN-QUESTIONS.md #8.

   Mint on this band is at ~1.2:1 (mist) — OPEN-QUESTIONS.md #1 — so the
   rule and the block's left border use `--kd-mint-2`, and the Kicker is
   called with `tone="light"`.
   ============================================================ */
import { home } from "../data/home";
import Kicker from "./Kicker.astro";

const { about } = home;
---

<section class="bg-kd-mist py-96">
  <div class="max-w-kd mx-auto px-24 sm:px-48">
    <div
      class="flex flex-col gap-48 min-[1120px]:flex-row min-[1120px]:items-center min-[1120px]:gap-0"
    >
      <div class="min-[1120px]:flex-1 min-[1120px]:min-w-0">
        <blockquote class="max-w-560">
          <p class="font-display text-d3 text-kd-ink" data-edit="home.about.quote">
            {about.quote}
          </p>
        </blockquote>

        <span class="block w-48 h-1 bg-kd-mint-2 mt-32" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>

      <div class="w-560 max-w-full shrink-0 border-l border-l-kd-mint-2 pl-40">
        <Kicker label={about.kicker} editKey="home.about.kicker" tone="light" />

        <p class="text-body text-kd-slate-2 mt-16" data-edit="home.about.body1">
          {about.body1}
        </p>
        <p
          class="text-body-sm text-kd-slate-2 mt-24"
          data-edit="home.about.body2"
        >
          {about.body2}
        </p>

        <dl class="mt-40 grid grid-cols-2 gap-24">
          {
            about.stats.map((stat, i) => (
              <div class="border-t border-t-kd-divider-light pt-16">
                <dd
                  class="font-display text-d6 text-kd-ink"
                  data-edit={`home.about.stats.${i}.value`}
                >
                  {stat.value}
                </dd>
                <dt
                  class="text-label-sm text-kd-slate mt-6"
                  data-edit={`home.about.stats.${i}.label`}
                >
                  {stat.label}
                </dt>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
